1
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:11,659
Nerdearla brings speakers from all over the world. But not everyone in the room understands English.

2
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:19,312
Sofi scans a QR code, chooses her room and her language.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,855
And this is not an animation: it's the talk, transcribed and translated live.

4
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:42,337
Also the other way around: from Spanish to English.

5
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:52,241
One room, five, ten: each one with its subtitles, at the same time.

6
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:01,823
The organizer connects the audio of each room and launches it with a single command.

7
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:11,919
And a panel notifies them if any room goes mute.

8
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:21,101
It learns the names from the agenda, speaks more languages, and exports the subtitles.

9
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:32,265
Oh, and the English subtitles of this video were translated by the project itself.

10
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,230
Live subtitles. Open source, for any conference.
